==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 2~4 seconds<sup>60f~120f</sup>.
*1 [[Great Ape Luza]] spawns as the boss after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*5 [[Formicidaean Ariant]]s spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 40~43.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,300f</sup>.
*100 [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.
*20 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
*1 [[Cumulus Gallus]] spawns after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.
*5 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 23.33~30 seconds<sup>700f~900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 83.33 seconds<sup>2,500f</sup>, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage relies on filling the entire field with small peons, then spawning threatening ones that allow the two bosses to push and eat away at any ground gained. With everything spawning on a timer, it's crucial to strike fast and hard earlier on, then defend viciously without letup, hopefully outlasting the onslaught to achieve victory.

===Recommended Units===
*[[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]] - Haniwa is a cheap meatshield with resistance to Traitless enemies and Behemoth Slayer. It falters against everything else, but considering the prevalence of traitless threats, Haniwa is still good to bring for stalling them. At level 43 or above, Haniwa's matchup gets even better as it is able to survive one strengthened hit from a 100% Cumulus Gallus, allowing it to bait another attack and keep the field clogged.
*[[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Reborn Warrior Doguemon]] - This unit, though a midranged tank with decent damage output on its own, works for the same reason as Haniwa, being resistant to Traitless and Relic threats with Behemoth Slayer and Curse Immunity. Most enemies within this stage are within its target traits, and its powerful attacks can leave a dent in all of the Behemoths here. It does require a bit of support against Formicidaean Ariant, however, as it has a fairly long delay between attacks and a slow animation.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]] - Doron is a suicide unit that destroys himself after one attack, but his massive health ensures he'll get there and spawn his level 3 Surge Attack. Being Immune to Curse, his 5-second Freeze and Knockback against Relics are both extremely helpful in delaying Great Ape Luza, and considering most Behemoths in this stage are vulnerable to Surges, Doron is also able to land some serious damage on them. He must be used with caution, however, as his cooldown is fairly long.
*[[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]] - Naala is Strong Against Relics, with 100% chance of a 4-second weaken to 50% and Behemoth Slayer, all of which mesh exceptionally well with its far-reaching LD attacks that can snipe and cripple Luza behind the lines, with everything else never escaping its wrath. Even if Naala's own low standing range is factored in, peons in the stage often allow it to exploit its LD at ease.

==Trivia==
*The enemy base is similar to that of the [[Empire of Cats]] [[Moon (Empire of Cats)|Moon]] stage.
*This stage reuses music from [[The Big Bang (Cats of the Cosmos)|The Big Bang]].
*This is one of the only stages in the game to have a chance of rewarding a [[Battle Items#Treasure Radar|Treasure Radar]], the others being [[Villains Jungle]], [[Unkept Promises]], [[An Ancient Curse]], [[Aku Altar's Seal]], [[Reign of the Ape Lord]] and [[Birth of True Man]].

